{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>ונתנו לאבי הנערה.</b> All are deficient (spelled without vav) except this one, for here it is plene (spelled with vav), like one who finds peace." "<b>לא יוכל לשלחה.</b> Even though other men are believed regarding their wives if they find in them an indecency — this man is not believed, but only by witnesses, since he has been established as a liar. Another interpretation: they measure against him measure for measure. He sought to forbid her to himself and to send her away from himself — therefore <b>לא יוכל לשלחה</b>. And likewise in the case of one who rapes, because sometimes he marries her against her will; therefore it is certain that he will divorce her if he can, and all his days are in standing and turning back."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:52.825089394Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}